{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"The mcp service sets none of the four gate-scratch settings; they exist only under review-bot. Adding them here makes compose the single source the autodeploy run path and the parity test pin against."},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"mcp_run_new creates the live blue-green MCP containers and sets none of the four settings, so gate snapshots land on the container writable layer."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py","reason":"Existing parity test pinning the gate-scratch mount across compose, terraform and observability.sh, but only for the service that already had the settings. Extended to cover the compose mcp service and autodeploy's MCP run path."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1789697339447288870,"uuid":"38b707eb-483a-422c-a787-ac31fd1f4337"}